  "code_forensics": {
    "root_cause": "Preflop evaluation fallback defect in eval_7cards wrapper",
    "defect_mechanism": "In Texas Hold'em preflop, there are 0 community board cards (len(all_cards) == 2). eval_7cards requires 5 to 7 cards. Both bots implemented a defensive guard: 'cat = eval_7cards(all_c)[0] if len(all_c) >= 5 else 7'. Because len(all_c) is always 2 on preflop, cat was identically assigned to 7 (One pair default).",
    "adaptive_preflop_branch": "AdaptiveHistoryExploiter line 65: 'if cat <= 6: ... if to_call < 200: return 1; return 0'. When facing a preflop raise (to_call >= 200), cat=7 causes 'cat <= 6' to be False, and 'to_call < 200' to be False -> returns 0 (Fold).",
    "multisizing_preflop_branch": "DynamicMultiSizingBot line 98: 'if cat <= 2: ... if cat <= 6: ... if to_call <= 100: return 1; return 0'. When facing a preflop raise (to_call >= 200), cat=7 causes cat<=2 False, cat<=6 False, to_call<=100 False -> returns 0 (Fold).",
    "conclusion": "Both classes produced 100% identical preflop action sequences (Fold on any raise), causing the entire game tree to branch identically."
  },
